#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186151901 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f63580eb-b476-51fa-a005-560f6e57d911" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Image of a Point Under a Linear Transformation of a Plane"}] :question/id #uuid "d2dafa69-6a9b-5f99-a16d-5fe5529ffd66" :question/math-academy-id "e-6704" :question/problem "Consider the linear transformation $\\mathbf T$ with matrix representation $T$, given by\n\n$\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 1 \\\\ -4 & -1\\end{bmatrix}$\n\nWhat are the coordinates of the point $B'$, the image of $B(2,-3)$ under the action of $\\mathbf T$?" :question/worked-solution "To find the image of $B$ under the action of $\\mathbf T$, we first create a column vector $\\mathbf{x}$ containing the coordinates of $B{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $\\mathbf{x}$ under the action of $\\mathbf T$ by calculating the matrix product $T\\mathbf{x}$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nTx &= \\begin{bmatrix}3 & 1 \\\\ -4 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe result, $T \\mathbf{x}$, contains the coordinates of $B'$. Therefore, $B'(3,-5)$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186151902 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "15e8730b-c59a-5897-8c83-073b54f517a9" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Image of a Line Given by an Equation in Standard Form"}] :question/id #uuid "2195a964-074f-5beb-abcd-ba0229e2872b" :question/math-academy-id "e-6705" :question/problem "Consider the line $5x-y-3=0$ and linear transformation $\\mathbf T$ with matrix representation $T$, given by\n\n$\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}$\n\nWhat is the equation of the image of the line under the action of $\\mathbf T$?" :question/worked-solution "First, let's find two points on the given line. Solving for $y$, we get $y=5x-3$, and substituting $x=0$ and $x=1$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}x = 0 & → y = 5(0) - 3 =-3, \\\\ x = 1 & → y = 5(1) - 3 = 2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nSo we have two points on the line, $P(0,-3)$ and $Q(1,2)$.\n\nTo find the images of $P$ and $Q$ under the action of $\\mathbf T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing the coordinates of $P$ and $Q$ in its columns:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ -3 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under the action of $\\mathbf T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nTX &= \\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ -3 & 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}-3 & -1 \\\\ -6 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective image points are $P'(-3,-6)$ and $Q'(-1,3)$.\n\nFinally, we write the equation of the line that passes through $P'$ and $Q'$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny - y_{1} &= \\frac{y_{2} - y_{1}}{x_{2} - x_{1}}(x - x_{1}) \\\\\ny - (-6) &= (3 - (-6))/(-1 - (-3))(x - (-3)) \\\\\ny + 6 &= \\frac{9}{2}(x + 3) \\\\\n2y + 12 &= 9x + 27 \\\\\n9x - 2y + 15 &= 0\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186151903 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0c8f0fa1-a86a-577f-bdc9-fc7427faa18d" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Image of a Line Given by an Equation in Slope-Intercept Form"}] :question/id #uuid "2192176c-e983-5913-b159-4d2bffd72ae1" :question/math-academy-id "e-6713" :question/problem "Consider the line $y=3x-2$ and linear transformation $\\mathbf T$ with matrix representation $T$, given by\n\n$\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$\n\nWhat is the equation of the image of the line under the action of $\\mathbf T$?" :question/worked-solution "First, let's find two points on the given line. Substituting $x=0$ and $x=1$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}x = 0 & → y = 3(0) - 2 =-2, \\\\ x = 1 & → y = 3(1) - 2 = 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nSo we have two points on the line, $P(0,-2)$ and $Q(1,1)$.\n\nTo find the images of $P$ and $Q$ under the action of $\\mathbf T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing the coordinates of $P$ and $Q$ in its columns:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under the action of $\\mathbf T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nTX &= \\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}0 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective image points are $P'(0,-2)$ and $Q'(-1,4)$.\n\nFinally, we write the equation of the line that passes through $P'$ and $Q'$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny - y_{1} &= \\frac{y_{2} - y_{1}}{x_{2} - x_{1}}(x - x_{1}) \\\\\ny - (-2) &= (4 - (-2))/(-1 - 0)(x - 0) \\\\\ny + 2 &= -6x \\\\\n6x + y + 2 &= 0\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152692 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f63580eb-b476-51fa-a005-560f6e57d911" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Image of a Point Under a Linear Transformation of a Plane"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8251953a-49f4-5d26-b78f-9ba3efd9e7c2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2, 1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186151063} {:answer/id #uuid "d2cd5e1b-08d6-58af-b649-3bbf6df34b6b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-2, 1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186151064} {:answer/id #uuid "d7eac83e-4d47-504a-bd45-d040debd9599" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(0, 2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186151065} {:answer/id #uuid "d938875d-57fc-5cb2-b2be-7a335a0f8c72" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1, 0)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186151066} {:answer/id #uuid "565b989b-4cf7-5c96-badd-cfbcc40aa4a3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-2, 0)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186151067}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8251953a-49f4-5d26-b78f-9ba3efd9e7c2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2, 1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186151063} :answer-field/id #uuid "cb370210-574f-55b5-a16d-2ada03fa4058" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186151062}] :question/id #uuid "dd69ce92-0c38-503f-b13d-fc02108de3ac" :question/math-academy-id "q-77543" :question/problem "Consider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T$, given by\n\n$T = \\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}$.\n\nWhat are the coordinates of the point $A^{′}$, the image of $A(-1, 1)$ under the action of $T$?"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152693 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "15e8730b-c59a-5897-8c83-073b54f517a9" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Image of a Line Given by an Equation in Standard Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d23ba586-378e-5d3d-9800-49c142ec7cc0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x + 2y - 3 = 0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186151069} {:answer/id #uuid "d9c400f5-ffc6-5b06-8733-44ea03b955fb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x + y - 3 = 0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186151070} {:answer/id #uuid "f7b7e19c-df6a-5549-9afb-e1f1509d522a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x - y + 12 = 0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186151071} {:answer/id #uuid "60a504e1-1b3b-59d4-a02f-5557157245c2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x + 3y - 6 = 0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186151072} {:answer/id #uuid "72c51eed-7c9c-5df8-a245-e2fb091242a9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3x - 2y + 12 = 0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186151073}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "72c51eed-7c9c-5df8-a245-e2fb091242a9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3x - 2y + 12 = 0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186151073} :answer-field/id #uuid "5a87469d-70fc-5df6-90b8-873b57bce2cd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186151068}] :question/id #uuid "e32e993e-cfb5-51a2-b706-960009cef89a" :question/math-academy-id "q-77653" :question/problem "Consider the line $2x + y - 3 = 0$ and linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T$, given by\n\n$T = \\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}$.\n\nWhat is the equation of the image of the line under the action of $T$?"}]}
